  "question": {
    "text": "A black body of temperature $T$ is inside chamber of temperature $T_0$. Now, the closed chamber is slightly opened to sun such that temperature of black body $(T)$ and chamber $\\left(T_0\\right)$ remains constant.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/nmdq3Fzc9vK4geUz_PKd_J9H2Qd2sBve2ZFny1StM6U.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rOrh5",
      "text": "\nBlack body will absorb more radiation\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1vloJ",
      "text": "\nBlack body will absorb less radiation\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EcCmT",
      "text": "\nBlack body emit more energy\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gOj2J",
      "text": "\nNone of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, the temperature of black body is constant, total heat absorbed $=$ total heat radiated.",
    "image": null
